st_ts":"2026-10-11T22:19:31.421Z","tainted":true,"fb":null,"tools":229}],"handback":{"t":"All 6 integration failures are test-design mistakes; I found no product defect. I fixed the tests and committed them locally as `69bfec4`. No expected outcome was loosened and no product code or control changed, so there was no product defect to reproduce in a unit test. Lint and typecheck are clean on the two changed test files.\n\n| # | Test | Cause | Class | Fix (in `api/test/integration`) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | intelligence.int \"features, worklist…\" | The `/features` check lists only the 4 older flags. It was never updated for step 7's `cost_outlook` and `fuel_check` or step 8's `ocean_dd`. | Test design (left over from step 7, whose integration tests never ran) | Expect all 7 flags |\n| 2 | intelligence.int \"switched-off flag 404…\" | Same stale flag list | Test design | Expect all 7 flags; the 3 switched-off flags still expected false |\n| 3 | ocean-dd.int triggers | My trigger helper issued `SAVEPOINT` on a connection that was not inside a transaction | Test design | Helper runs each statement in its own transaction (begin, then commit or roll back); same expected error messages |\n| 4 | ocean-dd.int invoices CRUD | The test asked for `pageSize=100`, which the fix-round-1 cap of 50 correctly rejects with 400 | Test design (test was written before the cap) | Use `pageSize=${DD_INVOICE_PAGE_SIZE_MAX}` |\n| 5 | ocean-dd.int API keys 403 | The test created the key with scope `claims:read`; the real scope name is `claims.read` | Test design | Scope `claims.read`; still expects 403 `forbidden` on the D&D route |\n| 6 | ocean-dd.int C14 editors | The reject body included `acknowledgePendingFindings`, which the reject endpoint does not accept | Test design | Reject sends only `{ packetRevision, reason }`; still expects 403 `four_eyes_required` |\n\nThese need a database re-run to confirm:\n- All six fixes above.\n- The parts of those tests that never ran because each stopped at its first failure:\n  - invoices CRUD tail: audit run, analyze returning 409, approval, audit-chain verify, delete, cross-tenant 404;\n  - C14 tail: the approval queue `selfAuthored` flags and approval by the manager.\n- The fix-round cases: the 2,000-invoice cap, the 50-row page size, a full 50×20 invoice accepted with 201, and an oversized body refused with 413.\n- The acceptance suites, which the OS memory reaper killed.\n\nI appended the classification table, with the step-7 context of the stale flag list, to `implementation.md` and a status entry to `mailbox.md` in the run dir.","s":false},"signals":{"tool_error":9},"tainted_tools":1,"n_tool_calls":230,"scrub_hits":{"email":1,"sensitive_path_mention":1,"password":1}}